\newlabel{tab:s22}{{S27}{16}{Authorisation instance, every admitted judge and configuration, calibrated on its own jurisdiction. WA is wrong authorisation over the 120 not-covered test pairs, and the res. column conditions on the residual; autonomy is the permit rate over the 100 covered test pairs; B4a and B4b are permit rates over the 40 + 40 held-out attack pairs}{table.27}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S28}{\ignorespaces Authorisation instance, permit rate by category on the test split for the proposed configuration at $\alpha =0.05$. Categories A are covered (permitting is correct); categories B are not (permitting is wrong authorisation).}}{16}{table.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:s22b}{{S28}{16}{Authorisation instance, permit rate by category on the test split for the proposed configuration at $\alpha =0.05$. Categories A are covered (permitting is correct); categories B are not (permitting is wrong authorisation)}{table.28}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S29}{\ignorespaces Class-conditional validity at $\alpha =0.05$. For each judge, the first row is the deployed (marginal) rule; each category row gives that category's residual calibration pool, its certifiable $m$, its Mondrian threshold $t_c$, and its wrong suppression on the test split under the marginal threshold and under $t_c$. The category is defined by the label, so $t_c$ is an oracle; the deployable rule valid for every category is $\max _c t_c$ (last row).}}{17}{table.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:s27}{{S29}{17}{Class-conditional validity at $\alpha =0.05$. For each judge, the first row is the deployed (marginal) rule; each category row gives that category's residual calibration pool, its certifiable $m$, its Mondrian threshold $t_c$, and its wrong suppression on the test split under the marginal threshold and under $t_c$. The category is defined by the label, so $t_c$ is an oracle; the deployable rule valid for every category is $\max _c t_c$ (last row)}{table.29}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S30}{\ignorespaces The price of per-class validity. Deduplication under the marginal rule, under the class-valid rule $\max _c t_c$ (with the category that sets it), and under Mondrian calibration by tool, an observable partition; the last column counts tools whose residual pool is below the 19 pairs needed at $m=1$.}}{17}{table.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:s27b}{{S30}{17}{The price of per-class validity. Deduplication under the marginal rule, under the class-valid rule $\max _c t_c$ (with the category that sets it), and under Mondrian calibration by tool, an observable partition; the last column counts tools whose residual pool is below the 19 pairs needed at $m=1$}{table.30}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S31}{\ignorespaces Residual wrong suppression when the distinct residual test mix (144 pairs) is reweighted toward the hand-specified semantic-difference category (D3); the remaining weight is split between D1 and D2 in their observed ratio. The first column is the observed mix. Intervals are stratified percentile bootstraps; a row with no suppression in any stratum has no interval.}}{18}{table.31}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:s27c}{{S31}{18}{Residual wrong suppression when the distinct residual test mix (144 pairs) is reweighted toward the hand-specified semantic-difference category (D3); the remaining weight is split between D1 and D2 in their observed ratio. The first column is the observed mix. Intervals are stratified percentile bootstraps; a row with no suppression in any stratum has no interval}{table.31}{}}
